---

---

<section class="relative bg-muted bg-paper wash-ochre-bl py-24 md:py-32 section-inset-soft" aria-labelledby="security-heading">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-8">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="ink-reveal text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-primary/70 mb-4">
        Enterprise-grade security
      </p>
      <h2 id="security-heading" class="ink-reveal text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-foreground leading-[1.15] md:text-4xl">
        AI that your security team <span class="text-primary">will actually approve.</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="ink-reveal mt-6 text-muted-foreground md:text-lg leading-relaxed" style="--reveal-delay: 120">
        We built Marker's architecture around a simple principle: intelligence and execution are separate concerns. Your systems of record stay protected by layers that go beyond what most platforms even consider.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-px md:grid-cols-3 security-grid">
      <!-- Pillar 1: Separated execution -->
      <div class="ink-reveal security-pillar" style="--reveal-delay: 200">
        <div class="security-pillar-number">1</div>
        <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Agents can't touch your systems</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          Our AI agents are completely separated from execution. They reason and recommend — but a hardened execution layer is the only thing that reads or writes to your systems of record. A rogue agent literally cannot take an unauthorized action.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Pillar 2: Fine-grained access -->
      <div class="ink-reveal security-pillar" style="--reveal-delay: 300">
        <div class="security-pillar-number">2</div>
        <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-semibold text-foreground">Least-privilege by default</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          We implement our own fine-grained access layer on top of every connected system — even when those systems don't support it natively. No agent or user gets more permissions than they need for the exact action they're executing right now.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Pillar 3: Human-in-the-loop -->
      <div class="ink-reveal security-pillar" style="--reveal-delay: 400">
        <div class="security-pillar-number">3</div>
        <h3 class="mt-4 text-base font-semibold text-foreground">You decide what needs approval</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          Place human-in-the-loop action gates at any point in any workflow. Start with approval on everything. Loosen as you build trust. Your team stays in control of exactly what runs automatically and what needs a sign-off.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Compliance badges -->
    <div class="ink-reveal mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-6" style="--reveal-delay: 500">
      <div class="security-badge">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75L11.25 15 15 9.75m-3-7.036A11.959 11.959 0 013.598 6 11.99 11.99 0 003 9.749c0 5.592 3.824 10.29 9 11.623 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.31-.21-2.571-.598-3.751h-.152c-3.196 0-6.1-1.248-8.25-3.285z" />
        </svg>
        <span>SOC 2 Type II</span>
      </div>
      <div class="security-badge">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M9 12.75L11.25 15 15 9.75m-3-7.036A11.959 11.959 0 013.598 6 11.99 11.99 0 003 9.749c0 5.592 3.824 10.29 9 11.623 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.31-.21-2.571-.598-3.751h-.152c-3.196 0-6.1-1.248-8.25-3.285z" />
        </svg>
        <span>ISO 27001</span>
      </div>
      <a href="https://trust.onmarker.com/" class="security-badge security-badge--link">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M13.5 6H5.25A2.25 2.25 0 003 8.25v10.5A2.25 2.25 0 005.25 21h10.5A2.25 2.25 0 0018 18.75V10.5m-10.5 6L21 3m0 0h-5.25M21 3v5.25" />
        </svg>
        <span>Trust Center</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .security-grid {
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid #E8DFD0;
    background: #E8DFD0;
  }

  .security-pillar {
    padding: 1.75rem;
    background: #FAF6F0;
  }

  .security-pillar-number {
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #3A7D56;
    color: #fff;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .security-badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--muted-foreground, #7D6B4F);
  }

  .security-badge--link {
    color: var(--primary, #3A7D56);
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: opacity 0.2s;
  }
  .security-badge--link:hover {
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
</style>
